course: dictionary
lesson: 653
title: Badly: poorly or seriously
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Badly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done or how much. It has two main meanings. The first is in a bad, poor or wrong way: «He played badly» means his playing was not good. The second is seriously or very much: «badly hurt» means seriously hurt, and «I badly want a dog» means I want one a lot.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to choose. «They watch him splash past, rolling badly but rowing his hardest.» Toad is not rolling well, so badly means poorly. Check by swapping in another word: «rolling poorly» still makes sense.
explain: «A hot drink can still scald a small child badly.» Here badly means seriously. Swap in «seriously» and the sentence still works. This meaning matters for safety, because a child who is badly scalded needs an adult straight away.
fact: Badly means in a bad, poor or wrong way, or seriously and very much.
fact: The comparative and superlative of badly are worse and worst.
fact: Phrases with badly: «badly off» means poor, «think badly of» means have a low opinion of someone, and «badly behaved» means not behaving well.
fact: «I did badly in the test» means I got a low score. The answer is to try again and practise.
fact: If someone is «badly hurt» or «badly burned», get an adult or emergency help at once. Do not wait to see if it gets better. The myth of putting butter on a burn is wrong: cool the burn with cool running water and get help.
exercise: «They watch him splash past, rolling badly but rowing his hardest.» In this sentence, badly means | *In a poor way | Very quickly | Very happily | Very loudly
exercise: «The child was scalded badly.» Here badly means | Politely | *Seriously, very much | Happily | Slowly
exercise: «I did badly in the test.» What does this suggest? | *I got a low score, so I should try again and practise | I did not take the test | I finished first and got full marks | I forgot my pencil
test: Which word is the comparative of badly? | *Worse | Badder | Badlier | Worst
test: «The burn blistered badly.» What does badly mean here? | *Seriously, very much | Slowly and quietly | Politely | In a happy way
exam: Which sentence uses badly to mean seriously? | «They walked badly home.» | «He tied his shoes badly.» | «She played badly in the match.» | *«She was badly hurt when she fell.»
